\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The charge matrix in the lattice transpose convention}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{In the basis of Igarashi and Pawlowski the conjugated
unitary link is #{U^C=(U^\dagger)^T=\bar U}, and their charge
matrix #{C_{\mathrm{IP}}} satisfies
#{C_{\mathrm{IP}}D(U^C)C_{\mathrm{IP}}^{-1}=D(U)^T}
\citet{§3, (3.1) and (3.3), pp. 3-4}{igarashi2009cp}.
In the direction from transpose to conjugated connection,
their intertwining matrix is #{C_{\mathrm{IP}}^{-1}}.
The matrix #{V_-} in \ref{fdip-017R} acts in that direction
for the centered operator. The spin transpose identity in
\ref{fdip-013T} compares their separate generator convention
\citet{§2, (2.4), p. 2}{igarashi2009cp}.
The site exchange and the fiber transpose in \ref{fdip-017S}
are additional operations on the field matrix.}
